{"doc_id":"DDC-059","file":"LINKS_DDC-059.tsv","header":["src_doc","src_page","text","n","kind","target_doc","target_page","target_page_end","target_pin","target_quote","status","by","note"],"rows":[{"src_doc":"DDC-059","src_page":"1","text":"Rule 6(b)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"13","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 6(b)","status":"verified","target_quote":"(1) In General. When an act may or must be done within a specified time, the court may, for good cause, extend the time: (A) with or without motion or notice if the court acts, or if a request is made, before the original time or its extension expires; or (B) on motion made after the time has expired if the party failed to act because of excusable neglect.","line":2,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-059-1-1-1-98382712","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":32,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-059","src_page":"1","text":"Fed. R. Civ. P. 25(d)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"38","target_page_end":"39","target_pin":"Rule 25(d)","status":"verified","target_quote":"An action does not abate when a public officer who is a party in an official capacity dies, resigns, or otherwise ceases to hold office while the action is pending. The officer's successor is automatically substituted as a party. Later proceedings should be in the substituted ... party's name, but any misnomer not affecting the parties' substantial rights must be disregarded. The court may order substitution at any time, but the absence of such an order does not affect the substitution.","line":3,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-059-1-1-1-1a08b225","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page":57,"target_pdf_page_end":58,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":